# Frozen Big-8 finding keys, one per line, as (file, line, cwe, category, message, severity).
# 154 keys were blessed from engine 94c5ee2 on the sha256-pinned corpus in gate_meta.json.
# Re-blessed to 136 keys on top of a191dcc: the
# library-identity gate now retires the torch/numpy.random numeric draws (and the
# torch.distributions draw its canonicalisation resolves) that were reported as CWE-338 in
# synthetic test data. Every retired line is LOW, CWE-338 and a numeric draw, and the
# adversarial boundary -- a credential drawn from those same libraries stays reported -- is
# pinned by benchmark/gates/cwe338_ml_math_probe.py, which no corpus can prove.
# Re-blessed to 119 keys on top of 62b11f8: the CWE-434 emitter now exempts local serialization.
# `TaintTracker._is_local_serialization_save` (ast_scanner.py) drops `<serializer>.save(...)` only
# when the canonical receiver names a serialisation namespace (`torch`, `torch_xla`, `smdistributed`)
# or is a model-card object, the module contains no upload sink, and no argument mentions a web
# source. All 17 retired rows are CWE-434, and each one - code, enclosing scope, payload and the
# binding of its destination - is documented in docs/cwe434_big8_fp_evidence.md. The must-report
# boundary is pinned by benchmark/gates/cwe434_local_serialization_probe.py: the 7 parity CWE-434
# uploads are `file.save(input())` in modules with no request object and are NOT retired, so
# aa_parity.py stays 425/425 MISSING=0 NEW=0. The 154 -> 136 rows above this block are untouched.
# Surviving rows are byte-identical to the 136-key file, in original order.
